<p>a) Prior periods results have been reclassified to conform to the current</p>
<p>	 presentation.</p>
<p>b) On October 1, 1996, AT&amp;T sold its remaining interest in AT&amp;T Capital Corp for about $1.8 billion, resulting in a gain of $162 million after taxes.</p>
<p>c) In the fourth quarter of 1995, AT&amp;T recorded a pretax charge of $3,029 million for restructuring costs of $2,307 million and asset impairments and other charges of $722 million. The total pretax charge was recorded as $844 million in network and other communications services, $934 million in depreciation and amortization, $1,245 million in selling, general and administrative expenses, and $6 million in financial services expense. The tax benefit associated with this charge was $993 million. In addition, charges of $1,172 million (net of tax) in the third quarter of 1995 and $2,145 million (net of tax) in the fourth quarter of 1995 are reflected in the loss from discontinued operations. These charges reduced 1995 income from discontinued operations by $3,317 million.</p>
